From 861c88ebfd9e22ace33e09c2b7addf4925792d59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:52:32 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] host pool: a POOL-backed expert table gathers in the prefill
 band by default (#131)

The pool arm's whole-table STAGING is the slow path at every width: its source is the pageable model
mapping plus the pool's host alias, and it degrades as pool coverage rises.  Measured on the 122B-A10B
across the three RDNA4 GPUs (-ncmoe 48, 5258-token prompt, -ub 2048, 2000-token greedy decode):

  arm                     prefill t/s   decode t/s
  pinned                     471.8         67.6
  pool FRAC 80               1502.6        67.1
  pool FRAC 95               1569.2        67.1

and with the gather forced OFF on the same arm, prefill collapses to 16.9 t/s -- so the staging path is
the defect and the device gather is the remedy.  At two devices the same change is neutral for pool
(948.6 vs 1024 staging) and leaves pinned untouched (1671.6).

GGML_SCHED_DEVGATHER becomes three-valued: UNSET = pool-backed tables gather in the prefill band and
everything else keeps staging (the new default); 0 = off (kill switch, the old behaviour); 1/force = the
historical A/B arm (gather below the staging width gate and for large tables, either host-expert mode),
which is NOT the default because it costs a pinned master ~47 % prefill at two devices.

Mechanism: a new optional device-iface query, moe_cache_pool_backed(backend, weight), answered by the
CUDA cache (is this table's master the read-only mapping rather than a pinned master) and forwarded by
the Meta backend to its simple devices.  sched_input_gatherable uses it to route a pool-backed table to
the gather; the band gate (n_tokens > moe_cache_band) keeps the decode/verify band on the arena
take-over, which the gather costs an order of magnitude (decode fell to 1.2-4.1 t/s without it).

Correctness: greedy text 257 chars sha=5531ae33f0f7 on all eight arms (pair and 3-GPU, gather auto and
forced), and 5835 chars sha=dc178c29fe89 across pinned / pool F80 / pool F95 at 3 GPUs with a 2000-token
decode behind a 5258-token multi-ubatch gather-served prefill -- i.e. the gather's prefill path is
text-exact at the width the old 'one-time expert-head zero' bug was in.  check-gpu-faults.sh clean.
